  "summary": "A Los Gatos planning commissioner, writing as a private resident, argues the town should keep and consider expanding its ALPR/Flock camera network, citing San Francisco's reported drop in vehicle break-ins and the potential expansion of Los Gatos-Monte Sereno police services into Saratoga. He acknowledges privacy concerns and a San Jose officer misuse incident but argues safeguards, not abandonment, are the right response.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I believe the Town should retain its existing ALPR network and consider expanding it where there is a demonstrated public safety need.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Reported theft-from-vehicle incidents fell from 19,841 in 2023 to fewer than 5,400 in 2025, a 73 percent reduction.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "But the officer was terminated, and San Jose subsequently tightened access to sensitive law enforcement systems and strengthened auditing procedures.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
